&Q000599 = Letter from Inim-Enlila to a king
@composite
#project: ucsl/etcsl
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.3.27
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.3.27&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div segment A

A.1. lugal inim sag₉-sag₉-ge diŋir-re-e-ne-er gub-ba
#lem: lugal[king]; inim[word]; sag[good]; diŋir[deity]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

A.2. ninda nidba si bi₂-sa₂ u₃-na-a-dug₄
#lem: ninda[bread]; nindaba[(food) offering]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. alan sukud-da dim₂-ma ad gi₄-gi₄ in-tuku
#lem: alan[image]; sukud[height]; dimma[thought]; ad[voice]; gi[turn]; tuku[acquire]
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. šag₄-la₂ sug₄ šag₄ kalam-ma dug₃-ga
#lem: šala[pity]; sug[full]; šag[heart]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. u₃-ne-de₃-tah
#lem: tah[add]
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. {m}inim-{d}en-lil₂-la₂ dub-sar dumu <{d}>suen-pa-lil₂
#lem: Inimenlila[1]PN; dubsar[scribe]; dumu[child]; Suenpalil[1]PN
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. arad-zu na-ab-be₂-a
#lem: arad[slave]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. nam-tag-ŋu₁₀ nu-zu nam-tag-ŋa₂ ŋeštug₂ la-ba-ši-ŋal₂
#lem: namtaga[sin]; zu[know]; namtaga[sin]; ŋeštug[ear]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. nam im-ri-a hi-iš₆-ši i-si-iš-bi ib₂-gu₇-en
#lem: nam[fate]; imria[clan]; heše[oppressed]; isiš[tears]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. ŋiri₃-pad-ra₂-ŋu₁₀ šag₄ iri kur₂-ra-še₃ a nam-ma-an-tum₃
#lem: ŋiripadra[bone]; šag[heart]; iri[city]; kur[different]; a[water]; tum[bring]
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

$ (unknown no. of lines missing)
@end segment

@div segment B

B.1. X X X šag₄# X
#lem: X; X; X; šag[heart]; X
#etcsl: line-id=B.1

#etcsl#doc may not be part of this composition

$ (unknown no. of lines missing)
@end segment








@translation labeled en project









@(A.1 = 1-7) Say to the king who entreats the gods fervently and, serving the gods, prepares the food offerings; repeat to the one elevated in stature who has the ability to give advice and counsel, the merciful one who makes the Land feel content -- this is what @wPN{Inim-Enlila} the scribe, son of @wPN{Suen-palil}, your servant, says:

@(A.8 = 8-10) I do not know my punishment: my punishment has not been considered yet. I am devoured by sorrow at the fate of the captive (?) families. Let my bones not be carried off by water to a foreign city.  @gap{unknown no. of lines missing} 



@(B.1 = 1)   @gap{1 line fragmentary}  @note{may not be part of this composition}  @gap{unknown no. of lines missing} 




